"da-14":[null,"79 assumes the newcomer scored the new mean — but they must PULL the mean up.","80 underestimates: raising 21 people's mean by 1 point takes 21 extra points, so 78 + 21 = 99.","Check: 1560 + 95 = 1655, a mean of 78.8, not 79."],
"da-15":[null,"21% is the total growth over BOTH years.","10.5% halves 21%, ignoring compounding — the annual multiplier is √1.21 = 1.10.","Check: 20% a year compounds to 44%, far past the actual 21%."],
